{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan-review remediation before claim: accepted both durability advisories. The commit phase now reuses check_no_rebase_in_progress before any staging and reuses the existing merge-recovery-blocked strict reason; best-effort warns and returns untouched. Default-mode lock/stage/commit failures are now explicit warn-and-return paths that never invoke push, retain content, and must support a clean retry; strict mode uses stable typed reasons. Added real recovery-marker, fault-injection, collateral-state, and clean-retry oracles. This preserves existing callers and vocabulary while preventing the new composite entrypoint from weakening store recovery."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786158796842712001,"uuid":"d5e10bf9-8842-4631-9e89-5f3ecb05f8a1"}